              "value": "Breath Weapon"
            },
            "action_description": {
              "value": "(acid, evocation, poison, primal)\n\nThe tarn linnorm can expel either a 120-foot line or a 60-foot cone of acid dealing 20d6 acid damage to creatures within the area (44 basic Reflex save). The acid creates toxic fumes. At the beginning of the linnorm's next turn, those who failed the breath weapon's Reflex save must succeed at a 42 Fortitude save or gain sickened 4 from the poisonous fumes. A tarn linnorm can't use Breath Weapon or Overwhelming Breath again for 1d4 rounds."
            },
